Acceleration of the system
$\begin{aligned}
a & =\frac{F}{m}=\frac{10}{2+3+5} \\
& =\frac{10}{10}=1 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{s}^2 \\
\therefore \quad T_1 & =(3+5) \times a=8 \times 1=8 \mathrm{~N}
\end{aligned}$

Given, $r=300 \mathrm{~m}, \mu=0.3$,
$g=10 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{s}^2$
If $v$ is the velocity of the vehicle while turning on the road, then
$\begin{array}{rlrl} 
& & \frac{m v^2}{r} & \leq \mu m g \\
\end{array}
$\Rightarrow  v \leq \sqrt{\mu r g}\Rightarrow v_{\max }=\sqrt{\mu r g}=\sqrt{0.3 \times 300 \times 10}=30 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{s}

Common acceleration
$\begin{gathered}
a=\frac{F}{m_1+m_2+m_3} \\
 a=\frac{40}{10+6+4}=2 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{s}^2
\end{gathered}$
Equation of motion of $m_3$ is
$\begin{aligned}
T_3-T_2 & =m_3 a \\
40-T_2 & =4 \times 2 \Rightarrow T_2=32 \mathrm{~N}
\end{aligned}$

Let $a$ be the acceleration of each block. Then,
$\begin{array}{ll} 
& T_3=\left(m_1+m_2+m_3\right) a...(i) \\
\text { and } & T_2=\left(m_1+m_2\right) a...(ii)
\end{array}
From Eqs. (i) and (ii), we get
$\begin{aligned}
T_2 & =\left(\frac{m_1+m_2}{m_1+m_2+m_3}\right) \times T_3 \\
& =\left(\frac{10+6}{10+6+4}\right) \times 40=32 \mathrm{~N}
\end{aligned}

$B$ will begin to slide on $A$, if pseudo force is more than limiting friction $F \gt F_1 \Rightarrow m\left(\frac{F}{m+M}\right) \gt \mu_s R\begin{array}{lr}
\Rightarrow & m\left(\frac{F}{m+M}\right) \gt 0.15 m g \\
\therefore & F \gt 1.764 \mathrm{~N}
\end{array}$
